Z||000005||BN Boomer||06-20-2000||02:58 PM||||Funny thing is, I don't Archie even ever addressed the issue of one of his employees supposedly taking one of his cars without permission. In all fairness, I don't think it should have ever been posted here in the manner that it was. This concern should have been expressed in private and if Archie blew it off or reacted poorly to a potential customers worries, then the rest of us could have been alerted to goings on at his shop.<P>If I were doing a V-8 conversion today, I'd probably want to use Archie's kit, but I'm not so sure I'd want my car spending any time at his shop, especially during the "testing" phase.<P>I don't think it was right to take shots at him like what happened, however. Not cool.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Sillhouette.com||06-20-2000||04:04 PM||||I think all of you voting to keep this Archie thing in private email are wrong.  Thaks to this forum (I owe you one Cliff) I have seen the true color of Archie and this forum has saved me 50G that I was ready to spend in my car for a Northstart mated to a Porche tranny conversion.  I was researching Archie to see how good he is and he failed miserably.  <BR>Also when one researches a company you don't go to the actual company to research it.  You go to people who actually had dealing with that company to get an unbiast oppinion.  For 50 G I like to have everythig done the way I want it.  That is the way new business is done.  The antequated way of who cares I got other clients has died a long time ago.<BR>Once again thanks for the forum Cliff.<P>Later||||reg||6
