Z||000010||Sillhouette.com||06-20-2000||08:43 PM||||I don't make my living of the website that I run.  It is safe to say that I made absolutely no money of anything there.  I'm a test pilot and seeing how it's inherently dangerous they pay very well and work you very little. You should see the life insurance that they give me.  <BR>The 50G comes from my wanting to buy a viper specifically 1995 RT10 however I found that everyone has one of those and modifying one of those is not a big deal.  Now to get a Fiero to put out some descent power is a challange and a lot of people don't know what a fiero is.  I already spent 10 G on the car that includes the purchasing price and I had the money aside for a 60G Viper.  Sorry if that got a bit long but that is a bit about me.  <P>Later<P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Haze_Performance||06-21-2000||12:47 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BN Boomer:<BR><B>Funny thing is, I don't Archie even ever addressed the issue of one of his employees supposedly taking one of his cars without permission. In all fairness, I don't think it should have ever been posted here in the manner that it was. This concern should have been expressed in private and if Archie blew it off or reacted poorly to a potential customers worries, then the rest of us could have been alerted to goings on at his shop.<P>If I were doing a V-8 conversion today, I'd probably want to use Archie's kit, but I'm not so sure I'd want my car spending any time at his shop, especially during the "testing" phase.<P>I don't think it was right to take shots at him like what happened, however. Not cool.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I must defend myself. The original post was not the topic of controversy. I posted what I saw…That’s it.   Then someone (That I believe to be from this forum) sent me a very disturbing email. The email in short said that I shouldn’t have informed Archie at all. If people didn’t like Archie they shouldn’t have posted anything in my original post. The right thing to do would have been to post there own topic about Archie. My feeling on my original post stands. It was a valid post about something that I saw. I never encouraged or added any opinions to the disagreements that were posted. I don’t know what you mean by saying, “In all fairness, I don't think it should have ever been posted here in the manner that it was” What manner? I attempted to contact Archie by phone all day. But with no luck I decided to post it as a topic, In hopes that someone might be able to contact him.    <P>Thank You<BR>Carl<P><BR>||||reg||2
